            <div xml:id="d571">

                <pb facs="0785" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.7111/284</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Rumanian Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davila</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-11-05">November 5, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my previous note No. 3376/P–31
                    of October 9, 1934, and Your Excellency’s note of October 23, 1934, I have the
                    honor to enclose an order<anchor n="1" xml:id="d571-f1"/> by the State Board of
                    Public Roads of Rhode Island against my chauffeur, Albert A. Amiaud, whose right
                    to operate motor vehicles within that State has been suspended. I will be
                    obliged to Your Excellency if you will intervene with the aforesaid authorities
                    to have this order rescinded, for the reasons set forth in my note of October
                    9th, as soon as possible, inasmuch as I feel that the attitude taken by the
                    authorities of Rhode Island has been most unreasonable and unjust.</p>
                <p>I take the liberty of drawing your attention to the fact that in the enclosed
                    order, it is stated that Amiaud has paid a fine of $1.00 and $5.00 respectively,
                    although the truth is that the amount he paid was $1.00 and $25.00
                    respectively.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles A. Davila</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
